questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a microservice intermittently hangs and exhausts its worker threads during peak traffic. A team member implemented a custom routing cache with hierarchical fallback logic using `ConcurrentHashMap`:

java
@Component
public class DynamicRoutingTable {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, RouteNode> routeCache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public RouteNode getOrComputeRoute(String sourceCluster, String targetService) {
        String cacheKey = sourceCluster + "::" + targetService;
        return routeCache.computeIfAbsent(cacheKey, key -> {
            RouteNode directRoute = resolveDirectRoute(key);
            if (directRoute == null) {
                // Fallback to cluster-wide default routing
                String fallbackKey = sourceCluster + "::DEFAULT";
                return routeCache.computeIfAbsent(fallbackKey, this::resolveClusterDefault);
            }
            return directRoute;
        });
    }
}
